1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:04,086
Your customers already check on their
tickets in your Help Center. What if they

2
00:00:04,086 --> 00:00:06,388
could act on them right there, with one
click?

3
00:00:06,468 --> 00:00:11,070
With Klick-Zen, you can add buttons to the
page where a customer views their ticket,

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:14,303
so they can confirm a fix, escalate, or
choose a next step.

5
00:00:14,383 --> 00:00:19,750
Start in Zendesk. Open the Klick-Zen app
from the left sidebar, and click Available

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,591
KlickButtons.

7
00:00:20,671 --> 00:00:24,872
Now the important part: turn on the "Help
Center Links" toggle. The Zendesk Help

8
00:00:24,872 --> 00:00:28,705
Center uses slightly different
placeholders than it does for triggers and

9
00:00:28,705 --> 00:00:31,593
automations, so the standard snippets
won't work there.

10
00:00:31,673 --> 00:00:36,298
Find the button you want, and click copy
beside its HTML snippet.

11
00:00:36,378 --> 00:00:41,624
Next, click the Zendesk Products icon in
the top bar, and select Knowledge. In your

12
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:46,807
help center, click Knowledge admin in the
top bar, then click the Customize design

13
00:00:46,807 --> 00:00:48,134
icon, the paintbrush.

14
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:52,737
A good habit: duplicate your live theme
and edit the copy, so you can preview the

15
00:00:52,737 --> 00:00:54,468
button before customers see it.

16
00:00:54,548 --> 00:00:59,224
On your copy, click Customize in the
corner of the theme preview, then click

17
00:00:59,224 --> 00:00:59,839
Edit code.

18
00:00:59,919 --> 00:01:06,267
Open request_page.hbs. That's the template
for the page where a customer views their

19
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:07,098
own ticket.

20
00:01:07,178 --> 00:01:11,205
Choose where the button should appear, for
example in the ticket details on the

21
00:01:11,205 --> 00:01:12,836
right, and paste the snippet in.

22
00:01:12,916 --> 00:01:17,020
One button is all that's needed for this
example, and you can always paste more

23
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:18,474
beside it to offer a choice.

24
00:01:18,554 --> 00:01:25,057
Keep it in request_page.hbs: the Help
Center placeholders only fill in on this

25
00:01:25,057 --> 00:01:25,474
page.

26
00:01:25,554 --> 00:01:29,984
Preview the theme, and open a ticket as a
customer to make sure the button shows up

27
00:01:29,984 --> 00:01:31,052
and links correctly.

28
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:35,777
When you're happy, publish the theme.
Every customer viewing their own ticket

29
00:01:35,777 --> 00:01:38,673
now sees the button, wired to their own
request.

30
00:01:38,753 --> 00:01:43,749
Here's your customer's view: their ticket,
the conversation, and one clear way to

31
00:01:43,749 --> 00:01:44,304
escalate.

32
00:01:44,384 --> 00:01:49,659
One click, and they land on a confirmation
page. No reply to write, and nothing else

33
00:01:49,659 --> 00:01:50,036
to do.

34
00:01:50,116 --> 00:01:55,176
Back in Zendesk, the ticket is already
marked Urgent, and no agent had to lift a

35
00:01:55,176 --> 00:01:55,619
finger.

36
00:01:55,699 --> 00:02:00,169
That's Klick-Zen in your Help Center:
one-click actions, right where customers

37
00:02:00,169 --> 00:02:00,914
already look.

38
00:02:00,994 --> 00:02:05,803
You can also use your own button image, or
show buttons only on certain tickets, such

39
00:02:05,803 --> 00:02:08,518
as open ones, using your theme's existing
logic.

40
00:02:08,598 --> 00:02:12,990
Find Klick-Zen on the Zendesk Marketplace,
and give your customers a faster way

41
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:13,435
forward.
